Access modifiers:
+   -->   Public
-   -->   Private
#   -->   Protected
~   -->   Package

Example of a Class UML diagram:
+-------------------+
|      User         | <-- Class Name
+-------------------+
| - userId: int     | <-- Attributes
| - name: String    |
| - email: String   |
+-------------------+
| + login(): void   | <-- Methods
| + logout(): void  |
+-------------------+

The attributes & methods follow the pattern --> attribute/method_name: return_type

For static fields & methods we simply underline it.

+---------------------------------------+
|            Employee                   |
+---------------------------------------+
| - id: int                             |
| - name: String                        |
| _- companyName: String_               |
+---------------------------------------+
| + getName(): String                   |
| _+ getCompanyName(): String_          |
| _+ setCompanyName(name: String):void_ |
+---------------------------------------+

For static fields/methods you can omit the access modifiers then that means the visibility is not shown.

Relationships:

Inheritance (▲)
Customer extends User

Association (—)
Customer places an Order

Aggregation (◇)
Order contains one or more Products

Composition (◼)


Multiplicity:
In UML, multiplicity (also called cardinality) shows how many instances of one class can be associated with another.

Example:
Customer 1 --------> 0..* Order
A customer can have zero or more orders. (* means infinite)

Note: Multiplicity is written at the opposite end of the arrow because it answers “How many objects of that class can one object of this class be connected to?”


<ins>Roles</ins>:
It answers "What role does this class play in this relationship?"
Customer 1 -------- 0..* Order
            orders
An customer orders many Order.



1. Association:
Customer -------- Order

Meaning:
Bidirectional association
Both classes know about each other
Navigable both ways

Customer --------> Order

Meaning:
Unidirectional association
Customer knows about Order
Order does NOT know about Customer



